│       producer role.
└── Load testing framework
    ├── Candidates : locust, k6
    ├── Used APIs  : Locust, constant, environment.events.request_success.fire, environment.events.request_failure.fire
    ├── Pitfalls   : Fundamental paradigm shift: Locust uses Python classes with event hooks; k6 uses JS scripts with built-in metrics; No 
    │   direct equivalent to Locust's environment.events system for custom request tracking; k6 does not support Python code reuse; the 
    │   KafkaClient wrapper would need full rewrite in JS; Different execution model: k6 uses VUs (virtual users) with iterators, not 
    │   class-based users
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── The code implements a custom Locust user class (KafkaLocust) for load testing Kafka producers. k6 can serve the same functional role
        (load testing) but uses JavaScript/TypeScript scripts instead of Python classes, requiring a complete rewrite of the test logic.

